% There is exactly one blank line between consecutive result blocks,
% whether or not a block has rows, so a block that
% matched nothing is still visible as its own gap: here the first and third
% queries are empty and the output is "", "", "a", "", "".  Reading it any
% other way -- for instance as "blocks are separated by a blank line only
% where both are non-empty" -- loses which query a row came from.
p(a).
q(b).

p(X), q(X)?
p(X)?
q(X), p(X)?
